  - first Hyde transformation and visual-language activation
  - short first-Hyde street behavior with beggar quick choice and optional destruction
  - live non-cutscene Rook approach with timed response choices
  - canonical first Rook knife wound and green-blood evidence
  - systemic Rook combat with no visible health-bar requirement
  - second penetrating Rook knife hit hard fail
  - inferred CONTROLLED / CHAOTIC / BRUTAL outcome telemetry
  - post-threat expressive Hyde choice and fixed Rook death
  - overnight fade and non-magical reversion resolution
  - Day-2 Poole wake/message
  - first Jekyll-home exploration and authored time pressure
  - bloodied-coat discovery via existing AuthorPacket state and hallway mirror route
  - clean/bloodied coat selection as K1-specific consequence interaction
  - author-lapse UI acknowledgment on missed coat danger
  - optional newspaper / optional ÚLEVA realization
  - initial Newcomen crime-scene consultation
