presentation_hooks:
  principle: Presentation reacts to state; it must not create new story topology or rewrite physical evidence.
  manuscript_time:
  - Day 1 laboratory/street/alley remains nocturnal.
  - Day 2 begins at 08:30 authored morning conditions while retaining AuthorWeather influence.
  - House clocks/windows/transitions may communicate K1LocalClockMinutes; permanent clock HUD is optional.
  - At 10:15 Poole reminder and at 10:30 leave pressure communicate authored time without a real-time countdown.
  first_experiment:
  - Potency/Purity may subtly influence serum appearance/handling without exposing raw stats before unlock.
  - Risky procedure must be described as an untested compound/additive, not CATALYST, to avoid collision with the base reagent
    category.
  transformation:
  - communicate pain, bodily discontinuity and form change
  - Distortion may alter intensity/style
  - must remain readable enough to teach the first transformation
  Hyde:
  - movement responsiveness and heavy physicality
  - camera/body language
  - impact feedback
  - form-specific constrained near-monochrome/duotone perception layer
  - authored RED semantic accents for violence/blood/immediate physical threat
  - authored GOLD accents for selected instinct-relevant objects/targets/cues
  - accent colors never auto-mark every interactable
  - Stevenson-derived weather/distortion remains visible beneath Hyde perception
  Rook:
  - live approach is not a cinematic; choice UI overlays gameplay
  - canonical first stab must read as Rook technique overcoming Hyde inexperience, not as Hyde being physically weak
  - green Hyde blood is clearly unnatural
  - no visible health bars
  - second penetrating knife hit must read as lethal danger
  - threat-active and threat-ended states must be visually distinct
  - fixed death beat must be separated from the moment Rook stops being a threat
  Day2_body:
  - Jekyll may instinctively touch/check the remembered wound area
  - 'skin is intact: no wound, no scar'
  - contrast with damaged/bloodied coat is a core observation
  coat_clue:
  - 'RICH: knife tear and green stain are directly readable in close wardrobe presentation'
  - 'THIN: mirror interaction is the authored reveal route'
  - 'FRAGMENTARY: mirror remains the minimum fair reveal route'
  - IMPAIRED cognition removes automatic Jekyll warning; the existing author-state debuff remains visible
  - no special glow/quest marker identifies the coat as evidence
  author_lapse_fail:
  - when Newcomen interaction begins in the bloodied coat, normal dialogue is interrupted
  - if the danger was never recognized, pulse the existing author cognition/debuff indicator
  - show blocking acknowledgment UI; player must click it before arrest sequence continues
  - the notice explains that Stevenson/Jekyll overlooked an obvious incriminating detail; exact final copy TBD
  newspaper_relief:
  - newspaper is optional and not objective-marked
  - if read, relief registers before any interpretation choice
  - if skipped, no substitute beat forces ÚLEVA
  research_journal:
  - pre-experiment journal reading is optional and consumes no manuscript time
  - Day-2 observations and canonical research tags resolve automatically at K1_RESEARCH_AUTO_UPDATE_DAY2
  - journal records brew method, first transformation, knife wound as Hyde and no matching Jekyll wound/scar
  - Research Journal and Research UI are accessed voluntarily through the game menu while Jekyll is playable
  - no sitting, physical journal interaction, manual writing or forced UI opening is required
  Jekyll_visual_rule: No K1-specific palette override. Use normal authored manuscript scene rendering.
