brew_choice_presentation:
  principle: PRECISE / FAST / RISKY are internal IDs only and must never be displayed to the player. The player chooses a
    concrete experimental procedure. Optional journal reading provides incomplete scientific context, not a correct-answer
    marker.
  raw_stat_visibility: Potency/Purity values remain hidden system values in K1. The master only unlocks better Potency/Purity
    estimation at ResearchProgress 20, so K1 must not expose exact brew numbers through normal player UI unless the master
    changes.
  options:
    K1_PRECISE:
      player_facing_intent: FOLLOW_RECORDED_PROCEDURE
      ui_copy_status: TBD
      journal_context: The current written formula is Jekyll's established baseline and is the most reliable preparation he
        has so far.
    K1_FAST:
      player_facing_intent: ATTEMPT_RAPID_PREPARATION
      ui_copy_status: TBD
      journal_context: An older margin note records Jekyll's untested idea that he should try preparing the reaction quickly
        sometime; it is a hypothesis, not a correction of a known mistake.
    K1_RISKY:
      player_facing_intent: INTRODUCE_UNTESTED_COMPOUND
      ui_copy_status: TBD
      journal_context: Jekyll has an untested idea that a trace of an additional experimental compound may strengthen the
        reaction, while its effect on stability is unknown.
  selection_rule: A player who ignores the journal may choose by intuition. A player who reads it receives authentic prior
    notes and hypotheses but still has to decide what to test.
research_journal:
  role: Diegetic research interface and persistent record of Jekyll's work. It carries pre-game scientific context, optional
    clues, current hypotheses and empirical observations so exposition does not need to be spoken aloud.
  pre_experiment_access:
    forced: false
    available_from: K1_PLAYER_HANDOFF_JEKYLL
    returns_to: K1_EXPERIMENT_GAMEPLAY
    contents:
    - Jekyll's purpose/theory for the experiment
    - selected prior attempts before the playable story
    - current written formula
    - baseline note supporting FOLLOW_RECORDED_PROCEDURE
    - untested note proposing rapid preparation sometime
    - untested compound hypothesis with unknown stability consequence
    exact_prose: TBD_DIALOGUE_OR_JOURNAL_CONTENT
    reward: INFORMATION_ONLY
    research_points: 0
  automatic_research_update:
    occurs_during: K1_RESEARCH_AUTO_UPDATE_DAY2
    trigger: K1Day2BodyObservationResolved == true
    player_input_required: false
    journal_open_required: false
    physical_journal_required: false
    time_cost: 0
    idempotent: true
    presentation: NO_FORCED_UI
    actions:
    - record the selected K1 brew method and its observed preparation result
    - record that transformation occurred while awareness persisted
    - record that Hyde survived one penetrating knife wound
    - record that Jekyll woke with no corresponding wound or scar
    - grant RD_BASE_TRANSFORMATION through ResearchSystem
    - grant RD_POST_TRANSFORM_PHYSIOLOGY through ResearchSystem
    - set K1BrewObservationRecorded = true
    - set K1ResearchGranted = true
    rule: >
      Resolve automatically when the Day-2 body observation completes.
      Sitting down, opening the journal, reading it or manually writing
      an entry is never required. The update does not open the Research UI,
      advance manuscript time or create a dedicated checkpoint.
      Research Journal access is already available from the first Jekyll handoff.
  method_dependent_observation:
    state_id: K1_BrewObservation
    persistent: true
    values:
      K1_PRECISE:
        observation_id: K1_OBS_RECORDED_METHOD
        meaning: The written baseline procedure produced Jekyll's cleanest/most stable K1 preparation.
      K1_FAST:
        observation_id: K1_OBS_RAPID_REACTION
        meaning: The rapid-preparation hypothesis is now empirically tested; activity remains useful but purity/stability
          is worse than the baseline.
      K1_RISKY:
        observation_id: K1_OBS_UNTESTED_COMPOUND
        meaning: The added experimental compound is now empirically tested; the response is stronger and markedly less stable.
    rule: This observation changes journal/research content and may be read by future authored research content. It does not
      by itself add an undeclared RD tag or extra ResearchProgress in v1.1.
  canonical_K1_research_awards:
    tags:
    - RD_BASE_TRANSFORMATION
    - RD_POST_TRANSFORM_PHYSIOLOGY
    timing: K1_RESEARCH_AUTO_UPDATE_DAY2
    note: The master currently declares these two K1 research tags. Method-dependent observations are recorded separately.
      If later we want PRECISE/FAST/RISKY to award RD_POTENCY_RESPONSE or RD_PURITY_RESPONSE directly, that must be added
      to the master.
  research_progress_ui:
    status: REQUIRES_MASTER_AGGREGATION_RULE_FOR_EXACT_NUMBER
    current_master_tag_values:
      RD_BASE_TRANSFORMATION: 10
      RD_POST_TRANSFORM_PHYSIOLOGY: 8
    expected_if_unique_tag_values_sum: 18
    next_master_unlock:
      threshold: 20
      effect: better Potency/Purity estimate
    rule: The UI may show research progress only through the canonical ResearchSystem resolver. Do not hardcode 18 in gameplay
      until the master explicitly defines ResearchProgress aggregation from resolved RD tag values.
  future_use: >
    The journal is player-openable from the game menu from K1_PLAYER_HANDOFF_JEKYLL
    whenever Jekyll is playable. Authored discoveries automatically update its
    pages/sections without requiring the player to open or read them.
